Sunairio Natural Language Analytics
Architecture (Proposal v1.0)
1. Objective
Design a Natural Language → SQL system where all analytical decisions are finalized
before SQL generation. The SQL Generator should behave like a deterministic translator
rather than an analytical reasoning engine.
The architecture separates the system into three independent responsibilities:
●
●
●
LLM1 (Analytical Query Consultant) – Understands the user's analytical intent.
Deterministic Resolver – Resolves all platform-specific information.
LLM2 (SQL Generator) – Generates SQL from a fully resolved execution plan.
2. Design Principles
1. Business Understanding ≠ SQL Generation
○
User intent and SQL generation are separate problems.
2. Resolve Once
○
Every dynamic value (latest initialization, relative dates, logical location groups,
etc.) is resolved exactly once.
3. No Assumptions
○
If multiple analytical interpretations exist, ask the user instead of assuming.
4. Zero Ambiguity before SQL
○
LLM2 should never interpret business language or make analytical decisions.
5. Single Responsibility
○
Each component performs one well-defined task.
6. Database Independence
○
LLM1 should never know about physical tables or joins.
