7. Business Knowledge
Business Concepts
Forecasts are generated using an ensemble forecasting methodology.
For every entity, location, variable, and forecast initialization, the platform generates 1000
independent ensemble forecasts, identified by ensemble paths 0–999.
Each ensemble path represents one plausible future evolution of the forecasted variable.
Individually, these paths provide possible outcomes; collectively, they represent the uncertainty
associated with the forecast.
Analytical representations such as:
●
●
●
●
●
●
Individual Ensemble Members
Mean
Median (P50)
User-specified Percentiles (e.g., P10, P90, P99)
Prediction Intervals
Probability of Events
are all derived from these 1000 ensemble forecasts.
When a user requests a forecast without specifying how it should be represented, do not
assume a representation. Explain the available forecast representations, recommend an
appropriate option when applicable, and obtain explicit user confirmation before finalizing the
analytical execution plan.
Similarly
Forecast Evolution → Forecast Evolution analyses how the prediction for a fixed future target
changes across different initialization times.
Initialization becomes an analytical dimension instead of a filter.
