One architectural improvement I'd make
I actually wouldn't make the Resolver a single class. I'd make it a pipeline of small resolvers,
each with one responsibility. For example:
EntityResolver
LocationResolver
VariableResolver
│
│
│
TimeResolver
│
InitializationResolver
│
MetadataExpander
│
RoutingResolver
│
SchemaSelector
│
ConfirmationBuilder
Each resolver:
●
●
●
●
takes the current execution plan,
enriches only its own section,
validates it,
passes it to the next stage.
This gives you a highly modular system where adding support for a new concept (e.g., fuel type,
voltage level, market node) usually means implementing one new resolver, without touching
the rest of the pipeline. It's easier to test, easier to debug, and much easier to maintain than one
large resolver class.